<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-peru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Peru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Peru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Alberto Fujimori closes Congress; Abimael Guzmán is captured</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-el-salvador"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20El%20Salvador.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of El Salvador</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Chapultepec Peace Accords end the civil war</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Commonwealth%20of%20Australia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Commonwealth of Australia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The High Court’s Mabo decision recognises native title</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20the%20Netherlands.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of the Netherlands</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Maastricht creating the European Union is signed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/czechoslovakia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Czechoslovakia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Czechoslovakia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The federation is dissolved peacefully on 31 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tanzania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Opposition parties are legalised</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-paraguay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Paraguay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Paraguay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A democratic constitution makes Guaraní an official language</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/ban-chiang-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ban%20Chiang%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ban Chiang culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ban Chiang becomes a UNESCO World Heritage Site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/saudi-arabia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saudi%20Arabia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saudi Arabia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King Fahd introduces the Basic Law in March; the Consultative Council of sixty appointed members is inaugurated in December 1993.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 27 April the Federal Council adopts the Constitution of the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia for Serbia and Montenegro, formally ending the breakup.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/aboriginal-australians"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aboriginal%20Australians.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aboriginal Australians</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the Mabo Case the High Court declares terra nullius invalid and recognises native title</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/guarani"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Guarani.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Guarani</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Paraguay’s new democratic constitution makes Guarani a language equal to Spanish</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/velvet-revolution"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Velvet%20Revolution.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Velvet Revolution</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Czechoslovakia splits peacefully into the Czech Republic and the Slovak Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/environmental-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Environmental%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Environmental movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United Nations Conference on Environment and Development meets in Rio de Janeiro</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/non-aligned-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Non-Aligned%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Non-Aligned Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The movement suspends the membership of Yugoslavia, a founding member, as the country breaks up</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/feminism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Feminism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Feminism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Rebecca Walker’s article “Becoming the Third Wave” gives the third wave its name</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/angkor-wat"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Angkor%20Wat.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Angkor Wat</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Angkor area becomes a UNESCO World Heritage Site, listed as in danger until 2004</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The constitution of 27 April establishes the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia as a federation of Serbia and Montenegro</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/santeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Santer%C3%ADa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Santería</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cuba's constitution is amended to declare the country secular rather than atheist</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/spiritism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Spiritism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Spiritism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The International Spiritist Council is constituted in Madrid on 28 November</span></li></ul></section>
